        "panel": {
          "introduction": "Dimorphos is the small moon of Didymos that NASA’s DART spacecraft struck in September 2022. This view preserves its encounter-era shape, reconstructed from DRACO and LICIACube images. DART changed its orbit and shape; this surface is not a model of the altered asteroid.",
